    {
      "title": "Values & data types",
      "level": 3,
      "scope": "locale",
      "intro": "",
      "columns": {
        "en": 0,
        "target": 1,
        "use": 2,
        "notes": 3
      },
      "terms": [
        {
          "en": "value",
          "target": "değer",
          "use": "tr",
          "notes": "Ordinary word.",
          "anchor": "term-value"
        },
        {
          "en": "number",
          "target": "sayı",
          "use": "tr",
          "notes": "Ordinary word.",
          "anchor": "term-number"
        },
        {
          "en": "true / false",
          "target": "doğru / yanlış",
          "use": "tr",
          "notes": "Not capitalised in prose. Keywords `true`/`false` stay English in code.",
          "anchor": "term-true-false"
        },
        {
          "en": "character",
          "target": "karakter",
          "use": "tr",
          "notes": "Naturalized, ordinary in technical prose.",
          "anchor": "term-character"
        },
        {
          "en": "integer",
          "target": "tam sayı",
          "use": "tr",
          "anchor": "term-integer"
        },
        {
          "en": "float / decimal",
          "target": "ondalıklı sayı",
          "use": "tr",
          "notes": "Use _kayan noktalı sayı_ only when the IEEE-754 floating-point nature specifically matters.",
          "anchor": "term-float-decimal"
        },
        {
          "en": "array / list",
          "target": "dizi",
          "use": "tr",
          "notes": "Exercise prose sometimes says \"list\" informally for the same concept; render both as _dizi_, do not introduce a separate word.",
          "anchor": "term-array-list"
        },
        {
          "en": "dictionary",
          "target": "sözlük",
          "use": "tr",
          "anchor": "term-dictionary"
        },
        {
          "en": "element",
          "target": "eleman",
          "use": "tr",
          "notes": "Array element = _dizinin elemanı_.",
          "anchor": "term-element"
        },
        {
          "en": "index",
          "target": "indeks",
          "use": "tr",
          "notes": "Deliberately not _dizin_, which means \"directory\" in filesystem contexts and would collide.",
          "anchor": "term-index"
        },
        {
          "en": "key-value pair",
          "target": "anahtar-değer çifti",
          "use": "tr",
          "notes": "The key itself is _anahtar_ (ordinary word once introduced).",
          "anchor": "term-key-value-pair"
        },
        {
          "en": "string",
          "target": "karakter dizisi",
          "use": "tr",
          "notes": "Real Turkish code and docs also show raw \"string\"; the glossary term is for prose.",
          "anchor": "term-string"
        },
        {
          "en": "data type",
          "target": "veri tipi",
          "use": "tr",
          "notes": "Chosen over Microsoft's more formal \"veri türü\" to match majority developer/tutorial usage.",
          "anchor": "term-data-type"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Functions & control flow",
      "level": 3,
      "scope": "locale",
      "intro": "",
      "columns": {
        "en": 0,
        "target": 1,
        "use": 2,
        "notes": 3
      },
      "terms": [
        {
          "en": "if statement",
          "target": "if deyimi",
          "use": "tr",
          "notes": "Keep `if` as the real keyword.",
          "anchor": "term-if-statement"
        },
        {
          "en": "condition",
          "target": "koşul",
          "use": "tr",
          "notes": "Ordinary/established word; stands alone.",
          "anchor": "term-condition"
        },
        {
          "en": "comparison",
          "target": "karşılaştırma",
          "use": "tr",
          "notes": "Ordinary word; stands alone.",
          "anchor": "term-comparison"
        },
        {
          "en": "expression",
          "target": "ifade",
          "use": "tr",
          "anchor": "term-expression"
        },
        {
          "en": "operator",
          "target": "operatör",
          "use": "tr",
          "notes": "Chosen over TDK's purist \"işleç\", which real developers do not use.",
          "anchor": "term-operator"
        },
        {
          "en": "NOT operator / logical negation",
          "target": "değilleme",
          "use": "tr",
          "notes": "In code context, the concept is \"`!` operatörü\"; the `!` symbol stays as-is in code.",
          "anchor": "term-not-operator-logical-negation"
        },
        {
          "en": "statement (executable)",
          "target": "deyim",
          "use": "tr",
          "notes": "The imperative sense: a line of code that does something and gets executed.",
          "anchor": "term-statement"
        },
        {
          "en": "statement (logical claim)",
          "target": "önerme",
          "use": "tr",
          "notes": "The proposition sense: a claim that is true or false; also a test assertion. Deliberately distinct from _deyim_ above.",
          "anchor": "term-statement-2"
        },
        {
          "en": "function",
          "target": "fonksiyon",
          "use": "tr",
          "notes": "The *keyword* `function` in code stays English; the concept in prose is _fonksiyon_. Chosen over TDK's purist \"işlev\", which real developers do not use.",
          "anchor": "term-function"
        },
        {
          "en": "to call (a function)",
          "target": "çağırmak",
          "use": "tr",
          "notes": "_fonksiyonu çağırmak_.",
          "anchor": "term-to-call"
        },
        {
          "en": "to define (a function)",
          "target": "tanımlamak",
          "use": "tr",
          "anchor": "term-to-define"
        },
        {
          "en": "parameter",
          "target": "parametre",
          "use": "tr",
          "notes": "Declaration-site name.",
          "anchor": "term-parameter"
        },
        {
          "en": "argument",
          "target": "argüman",
          "use": "tr",
          "notes": "Call-site value. Chosen over the more formal \"bağımsız değişken\", which real developers rarely use.",
          "anchor": "term-argument"
        },
        {
          "en": "input (to a function)",
          "target": "girdi",
          "use": "tr",
          "anchor": "term-input"
        },
        {
          "en": "output",
          "target": "çıktı",
          "use": "tr",
          "anchor": "term-output"
        },
        {
          "en": "to return (a value)",
          "target": "döndürmek",
          "use": "tr",
          "notes": "\"Bir değer döndürür.\"",
          "anchor": "term-to-return"
        },
        {
          "en": "return value",
          "target": "dönüş değeri",
          "use": "tr",
          "notes": "Noun form; keep distinct from the verb _döndürmek_ above.",
          "anchor": "term-return-value"
        },
        {
          "en": "pure function",
          "target": "saf fonksiyon",
          "use": "tr",
          "anchor": "term-pure-function"
        }
      ]
    },
